{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>They shall minister to you.</b> The meaning is, they shall be for your needs. Similar is 'the garments of the ministering [שרד] to minister in the holy' (Exodus 35:19) — these are the garments of the journey." "<b>They shall go up for acceptance upon My altar.</b> Now, על draws after it עמו [with it]; and so it is, על מזבחי."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 60, :notes {1 "The argument is compressed: על in יעלו על governs רצון just as על in על מזבחי does; rendered hyper-literally without expanding the grammatical point."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:00:26.968684232Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}